WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.341 --> 00:00:07.433
[Subtitles by danielsangeo]

00:00:10.663 --> 00:00:14.254
I'm not sure I really WANT
redemption from electro-Jesus.

00:00:14.254 --> 00:00:17.613
I mean, what kind of electric sins
is he going to forgive me for?

00:00:17.613 --> 00:00:19.069
Too much resistance?

00:00:19.069 --> 00:00:21.483
The human body doesn't use THAT much power.

00:00:21.483 --> 00:00:24.344
What's the brain? 20 watts?
Something like that?

00:00:24.344 --> 00:00:27.859
Okay, I guess we DID use a lot of
power conducting the experiment,

00:00:27.859 --> 00:00:29.815
and that sort of ended the world.

00:00:29.815 --> 00:00:32.600
So, yeah, I guess that one's on me.

00:00:32.600 --> 00:00:33.581
[zombie growls]

00:00:33.581 --> 00:00:34.081
Hup!

00:00:36.331 --> 00:00:40.404
I'm pretty sure that's not even why people
want to kill me, though. I'm just...here.

00:00:40.404 --> 00:00:42.513
I mean, we're talking different levels--

00:00:42.513 --> 00:00:43.381
Dammit.

00:00:44.024 --> 00:00:46.139
--different levels of wanting to kill me.

00:00:46.139 --> 00:00:48.789
[straining]
Obviously the people in this town

00:00:48.789 --> 00:00:52.791
want to kill me for different reasons
than in the city. I'm multicultural.

00:00:52.791 --> 00:00:57.233
Wow, so that was really it. He was
blocking the way with his corpse fire.

00:00:57.233 --> 00:00:58.166
Why?

00:00:58.166 --> 00:01:01.297
It doesn't scare them off.
It was just a propane tank;

00:01:01.297 --> 00:01:03.015
it was going to burn out by morning.

00:01:03.015 --> 00:01:05.751
That makes no sense if
you're not having a concert.

00:01:06.666 --> 00:01:07.820
[loud explosion]

00:01:07.820 --> 00:01:08.808
WOW!

00:01:08.808 --> 00:01:10.711
Making my OWN music.

00:01:10.711 --> 00:01:11.856
Well, not really.

00:01:15.347 --> 00:01:16.899
That would be better as a support.

00:01:17.261 --> 00:01:20.936
Like, you wait for a break in the song,
then blow up the barrel as it comes back.

00:01:20.936 --> 00:01:23.541
[imitating guitar riff]

00:01:23.541 --> 00:01:24.108
Explosion.

00:01:24.108 --> 00:01:27.510
[imitating guitar riff]

00:01:27.510 --> 00:01:29.104
My talent's wasted here.

00:01:29.104 --> 00:01:30.474
Just like the propane.

00:01:30.474 --> 00:01:33.973
Though, there IS a lot
of fuel in these parts.

00:01:33.973 --> 00:01:36.541
See? European Saudi Arabia.

00:01:36.541 --> 00:01:38.074
[loud explosion]
Whoa!

00:01:38.937 --> 00:01:40.720
Yeah, I'm making a lot of noise.

00:01:41.519 --> 00:01:42.356
But why are they...

00:01:43.506 --> 00:01:47.140
Why are they leaving fuel
drums in tight hallways?

00:01:47.140 --> 00:01:48.221
Another one!

00:01:48.795 --> 00:01:50.365
Okay, good.

00:01:50.365 --> 00:01:53.031
I wouldn't want--Are you KIDDING me?

00:01:55.135 --> 00:01:57.116
Jesus Christ!

00:01:57.116 --> 00:01:59.307
Well, I guess that would be a quick death.

00:01:59.307 --> 00:02:01.513
I pull the trigger, my aim's sloppy,

00:02:01.513 --> 00:02:04.547
a few milliseconds of a flash, then death?

00:02:04.547 --> 00:02:07.391
I mean, they had to
cart the barrels up here.

00:02:07.391 --> 00:02:10.958
That's a lot of work for...no reason at all.

00:02:10.958 --> 00:02:12.647
Oh what, is he faking?

00:02:13.043 --> 00:02:13.816
OH!

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:15.947
BASTARD!

00:02:19.591 --> 00:02:21.860
Can't assume a thing.

00:02:21.860 --> 00:02:24.550
So are they learning, or just lazy?

00:02:24.550 --> 00:02:28.897
I guess that's more positive than
being pissed off all the time.

00:02:29.328 --> 00:02:30.447
Oh no...

00:02:30.447 --> 00:02:32.652
So do I need to worry about you?

00:02:32.652 --> 00:02:34.622
Yeah, just lying there, huh?

00:02:35.296 --> 00:02:36.636
OH MY GOD!

00:02:38.098 --> 00:02:39.196
I'M OUT!

00:02:39.196 --> 00:02:41.825
Okay, so is this going to be a thing now?

00:02:41.825 --> 00:02:45.082
I have to shoot every
single body, just in case?

00:02:45.082 --> 00:02:47.508
That's who I am? I'm that guy now?

00:02:47.508 --> 00:02:50.269
That's not who I am. I don't
have that kind of ammo.

00:02:50.269 --> 00:02:51.172
[poison headcrab rattles, hisses]

00:02:51.172 --> 00:02:52.836
What the fuck?

00:02:52.836 --> 00:02:54.570
Like a rattlesnake.

00:02:54.570 --> 00:02:56.388
Holy shit!

00:02:56.388 --> 00:02:57.302
Nawww...

00:02:59.802 --> 00:03:02.105
Oh, good! They understand what I'm saying!

00:03:03.546 --> 00:03:05.685
Yeah, that's what was missing from my life--

00:03:05.685 --> 00:03:09.791
for these things to look more like
black widow spiders, and hiss at me.

00:03:09.791 --> 00:03:13.819
That really filled the void.
I guess this is a good day after all.

00:03:13.819 --> 00:03:15.492
Oh, so HERE'S the sw...

00:03:17.834 --> 00:03:19.830
Wait, did I turn it off?

00:03:19.830 --> 00:03:23.708
It stopped sparking, but
that doesn't mean it's off.

00:03:23.708 --> 00:03:26.063
I'm going to get out of
here before I start a fire.

00:03:26.063 --> 00:03:28.975
Though fires are less scary
when it's not YOUR house,

00:03:28.975 --> 00:03:30.792
so you don't care if it burns down.

00:03:30.792 --> 00:03:32.445
I'm not attached to this place.

00:03:32.445 --> 00:03:35.910
And neither was the owner. Maybe
that's why there were fuel drums here.

00:03:35.910 --> 00:03:40.933
Maybe the invasion interrupted an
insurance scam from a decade or two ago.

00:03:40.933 --> 00:03:42.787
There's not really--OH!

00:03:44.841 --> 00:03:46.829
Where are they coming from?

00:03:46.829 --> 00:03:51.344
Oh, they must've been hiding in the
generators, and I walked right by them.

00:03:51.344 --> 00:03:53.717
I can't b--OH MY GOD!

00:03:53.717 --> 00:03:56.590
No! I need you to promise me
you'll never do that again.

00:03:57.126 --> 00:03:58.066
Can you do that?

00:03:59.362 --> 00:04:01.492
Okay, I think I believe you.

00:04:01.492 --> 00:04:03.458
This is a trust exercise.

00:04:03.458 --> 00:04:05.178
This is me trusting you.

00:04:06.505 --> 00:04:09.004
On second thought, you were
making that hissing noise,

00:04:09.004 --> 00:04:10.964
and I think we both know that's not cool.

00:04:10.964 --> 00:04:14.701
So, sorry, you failed the
exercise. This is on you.

00:04:14.701 --> 00:04:17.423
Still kind of weird how
they drop down, though.

00:04:17.423 --> 00:04:19.792
Wow, they can't fly, can they?

00:04:19.792 --> 00:04:23.191
That would make the day
worse. More than a little bit.

00:04:23.191 --> 00:04:24.532
It's always something.

00:04:24.532 --> 00:04:27.010
I still don't know if I
even need to go this way.

00:04:27.010 --> 00:04:28.574
Yeah, if somebody could see me,

00:04:28.574 --> 00:04:31.821
they might ask why am I breaking
into a transformer station,

00:04:31.821 --> 00:04:34.215
and I would say,
"Fuck you. Why do anything?"

00:04:34.775 --> 00:04:36.036
Looks safe...

00:04:36.036 --> 00:04:38.470
Yeah, don't think they'd
have an answer for that.

00:04:40.126 --> 00:04:44.465
Yeah, it feels impossible, but
today actually could've been worse.

00:04:44.465 --> 00:04:48.013
During that nightmare this morning, 
I could've been teleported into a building

00:04:48.013 --> 00:04:49.618
and had my neck snapped.

00:04:49.618 --> 00:04:53.080
And we still don't even know
what caused the FIRST cascade.

00:04:53.080 --> 00:04:56.188
Maybe my body could've just
kept teleporting forever.

00:04:56.188 --> 00:04:58.561
I would've become a real-life haunting,

00:04:58.561 --> 00:05:01.258
because no one would ever know
when my body would show up.

00:05:02.482 --> 00:05:03.536
[man laughs maniacally]

00:05:03.536 --> 00:05:04.959
Ah ha ha ha ha ha...

00:05:04.959 --> 00:05:06.096
MAN: Well done, brother!

00:05:06.096 --> 00:05:07.074
Oh, you were watching.

00:05:07.074 --> 00:05:11.726
MAN: Make free use of my traps, but
take care not to fall in them yourself.

00:05:11.726 --> 00:05:13.275
Call me Mr. Trapeze.

00:05:13.275 --> 00:05:14.119
MAN: Behind you!

00:05:14.119 --> 00:05:14.993
What?!

00:05:14.993 --> 00:05:15.633
Where?

00:05:16.770 --> 00:05:17.633
OH!

00:05:17.633 --> 00:05:19.477
MAN: In Ravenholm, you'd
do well to be vigilant.

00:05:19.477 --> 00:05:21.315
The roof!

00:05:21.315 --> 00:05:24.759
Oh my god, this is embarrassing.

00:05:24.759 --> 00:05:27.394
Now he thinks I'm wet behind the ears.

00:05:27.394 --> 00:05:28.010
NYAH!

00:05:28.548 --> 00:05:32.029
I made TWO mistakes! Right in front of him!

00:05:32.029 --> 00:05:34.260
First mistake: I'm getting sloppy.

00:05:34.260 --> 00:05:38.071
I forgot that anything could kill
me from anywhere at all times.

00:05:38.071 --> 00:05:39.220
What's wrong with me?

00:05:39.220 --> 00:05:42.603
I don't get shot at for ten
minutes and now I'm turning soft?

00:05:42.603 --> 00:05:45.485
How many of these hunters
are dropping from above?

00:05:45.485 --> 00:05:47.153
It feels like a lot lately.

00:05:47.153 --> 00:05:51.348
Second mistake: He had a gun on
me, and I turned my back to him.

00:05:51.348 --> 00:05:54.524
He said, "Behind you!" 
I actually fell for that!

00:05:54.524 --> 00:05:56.310
That's something *I* would say!

00:05:56.310 --> 00:06:00.821
He may as well have told me my shoes
are untied! That's Looney Tunes shit!

00:06:00.821 --> 00:06:03.985
Okay, I need to land on the support
in case the boards are loose

00:06:03.985 --> 00:06:06.565
so they don't catapult
and smack me in the face.

00:06:08.126 --> 00:06:11.599
I bet he's filming this,
just in case I faceplant.

00:06:11.599 --> 00:06:13.767
Probably using a fisheye lens, too.

00:06:13.767 --> 00:06:17.060
Then he narrates it, saying,
"Watch out for the traps."

00:06:17.060 --> 00:06:18.450
Then the music starts.

00:06:18.450 --> 00:06:22.296
[humming bass line]

00:06:22.296 --> 00:06:24.058
How is that guy living here?

00:06:24.058 --> 00:06:24.624
I mean...

00:06:27.211 --> 00:06:32.613
I can see passing through, but in
SOME ways, this is worse than fleas.

00:06:32.613 --> 00:06:33.897
There's no--OH!

00:06:35.679 --> 00:06:39.239
Actually fleas are not mutually
exclusive to this situation.

00:06:39.761 --> 00:06:41.859
Is he trying to wait them out?

00:06:41.859 --> 00:06:43.744
Yeah, just what's going on here?

00:06:44.235 --> 00:06:46.117
How are they sustaining themselves?

00:06:47.618 --> 00:06:49.408
All I'm seeing are predators.

00:06:50.249 --> 00:06:51.202
I'm out!

00:06:51.202 --> 00:06:53.767
I mean, okay, they ate everyone in town;

00:06:53.767 --> 00:06:57.273
I haven't seen any dogs or
cats--they probably ate them, too;

00:06:57.273 --> 00:07:00.040
at some point, this party is going to end.

00:07:00.040 --> 00:07:01.508
Maybe he's counting on that.

00:07:02.361 --> 00:07:06.136
We're still in the honeymoon phase
while there's corpses lying around.

00:07:06.136 --> 00:07:07.746
[grunting]
But, eventually...

00:07:08.658 --> 00:07:10.685
...they're going to run out
of things to eat.

00:07:10.685 --> 00:07:13.436
Honestly, I'm doing them
a favor by shooting them.

00:07:13.436 --> 00:07:16.043
Now they have a fresh supply to cannibalize.

00:07:16.043 --> 00:07:16.989
You're welcome.

00:07:16.989 --> 00:07:19.990
I'm probably prolonging
all of this by months.

00:07:19.990 --> 00:07:21.298
What is this?

00:07:21.298 --> 00:07:22.240
Pull lever.

00:07:23.433 --> 00:07:24.188
OH!

00:07:24.188 --> 00:07:26.001
ATTACK OF THE K-CARS!

00:07:26.001 --> 00:07:27.176
NOT AGAIN!

00:07:27.176 --> 00:07:29.500
Wait, no, that's a European.

00:07:29.500 --> 00:07:30.081
Okay...

00:07:31.006 --> 00:07:31.506
Fuck.

00:07:33.817 --> 00:07:36.519
Well, so much for a quiet night.

00:07:36.519 --> 00:07:38.046
MAN: Better and better!

00:07:38.046 --> 00:07:41.756
Okay, he is definitely filming me.

00:07:41.756 --> 00:07:45.661
I don't see the cameras, but
there's a lot of places to put them.

00:07:45.661 --> 00:07:49.460
Oh, and of course. I'm in the
future. Who knows what they have now?

00:07:49.460 --> 00:07:53.052
They could have fiber optics all
over here and I wouldn't see a thing.

00:07:53.052 --> 00:07:55.925
Oh! Maybe that's how they were tracking me!

00:07:55.925 --> 00:07:58.141
I hope he's not broadcasting this.

00:07:58.141 --> 00:08:02.487
Of course I'll look good on camera,
but if the cops see me, then...

00:08:02.487 --> 00:08:04.684
They might just bomb the town.

00:08:04.684 --> 00:08:07.395
Or just drop nerve gas. That would be great.

00:08:07.395 --> 00:08:08.291
Please back up.

00:08:10.154 --> 00:08:12.289
Beep. Beep.

00:08:12.289 --> 00:08:13.471
Okay, let's do it.

00:08:14.363 --> 00:08:18.182
Huh. Well. That DID work,

00:08:18.182 --> 00:08:22.414
but I can't imagine something less
efficient without going full Rube Goldberg.

00:08:22.414 --> 00:08:24.532
But then that's not the point, is it?

00:08:24.532 --> 00:08:26.806
The point is,
this guy saw "The Running Man",

00:08:26.806 --> 00:08:29.318
and now he's living his dream through me.

00:08:29.318 --> 00:08:30.454
I get it now.

00:08:30.454 --> 00:08:33.685
Though this doesn't look developed
into a full game show yet.

00:08:33.685 --> 00:08:35.310
He must still be working on it.

00:08:35.310 --> 00:08:35.810
Hup!

00:08:37.681 --> 00:08:40.680
So my appearance was just a
lucky coincidence for him.

00:08:40.680 --> 00:08:44.030
So he's having me trial run his
course before he goes public.

00:08:44.030 --> 00:08:47.524
That's good, because that means
he's probably NOT broadcasting this,

00:08:47.524 --> 00:08:49.749
since it's not fit for presentation yet.

00:08:49.749 --> 00:08:53.559
He needs lights, music... probably
has to do a bunch of painting.

00:08:53.559 --> 00:08:55.165
So where the hell am I going?

00:08:55.165 --> 00:08:56.743
He needs to work on that.

00:08:56.743 --> 00:08:58.911
Yeah, I was giving him a 50-50 chance

00:08:58.911 --> 00:09:02.149
he was just going to keep these videos
for his private collection anyway.

00:09:02.149 --> 00:09:03.438
He seems like the type.

00:09:03.438 --> 00:09:05.189
So where does he expect me to go?

00:09:05.189 --> 00:09:08.069
Those catwalks are obviously
part of the course.

00:09:08.069 --> 00:09:10.366
Oh! It's like the old saying...

00:09:12.045 --> 00:09:14.306
"When is a car like an elevator?

00:09:14.306 --> 00:09:18.054
"Pretty much only this time ever."
This is so inefficient.

00:09:18.054 --> 00:09:19.438
Could be worse.

00:09:19.438 --> 00:09:21.441
I think he took out the engine block.

00:09:21.441 --> 00:09:22.193
GRIGORI: I am Father Grigori.

00:09:22.193 --> 00:09:23.940
Wah!
GRIGORI: I am Father Grigori.

00:09:23.940 --> 00:09:27.801
GRIGORI: You have already
met--heh heh--my "congregation".

00:09:27.801 --> 00:09:29.271
[Grigori laughs maniacally]

00:09:29.271 --> 00:09:31.885
[laughing maniacally]

00:09:31.885 --> 00:09:34.515
Damn, I don't remember the
ending to The Running Man.

00:09:34.515 --> 00:09:37.971
I know there were people trying to
kill him that were part of the show,

00:09:37.971 --> 00:09:41.290
but I can't remember if it was
rigged for him to lose or not.

00:09:41.290 --> 00:09:44.590
I kind of want to know that
considering my situation.

00:09:44.590 --> 00:09:47.239
That guy's probably seen
the movie a hundred times.

00:09:47.239 --> 00:09:49.871
I mean, he's taking some
creative liberties, but...

00:09:51.756 --> 00:09:54.222
Now I wonder how many
aliens were actually here,

00:09:54.222 --> 00:09:55.905
or if he was just trucking them all in.

00:09:55.905 --> 00:09:57.410
[shotgun blasts, Grigori laughing]

00:09:57.410 --> 00:09:59.961
So does he want to be the
contestant or the host?

00:09:59.961 --> 00:10:01.099
Sounds like both.

00:10:01.754 --> 00:10:02.944
FUCKING HELL!

00:10:02.944 --> 00:10:03.669
GRIGORI: Woe betide--

00:10:03.669 --> 00:10:05.003
[loud sigh]

00:10:05.003 --> 00:10:08.086
Oh my god... I heard that one...

00:10:08.086 --> 00:10:09.870
Almost took my head off.

00:10:09.870 --> 00:10:11.654
And I can't believe I'm saying this,

00:10:11.654 --> 00:10:13.572
but I think that was an accident?

00:10:14.708 --> 00:10:16.457
Yeah, he's not firing.

00:10:17.012 --> 00:10:18.740
Yeah, you're not trying to kill me,

00:10:18.740 --> 00:10:22.860
you're just not worried about any of
that "in the line of fire" bullshit, huh?

00:10:23.519 --> 00:10:26.767
GRIGORI: Ah! It is you, brother.
I apologize.

00:10:26.767 --> 00:10:28.297
GRIGORI: But, no harm done.

00:10:28.297 --> 00:10:28.814
Ehhh...

00:10:28.814 --> 00:10:31.420
GRIGORI: My bullets are
the least of your concerns.

00:10:31.420 --> 00:10:31.920
No...

00:10:35.661 --> 00:10:37.596
No, don't sell yourself short.

00:10:37.596 --> 00:10:39.355
You--oh, he's gone.

00:10:39.355 --> 00:10:41.937
You're right that you're
not my BIGGEST concern,

00:10:41.937 --> 00:10:43.404
but that little st--

00:10:43.404 --> 00:10:44.835
[Grigori laughs]

00:10:44.835 --> 00:10:47.345
Oh, so he CAN hear me. Well then...

00:10:47.345 --> 00:10:48.515
What the fuck?!

00:10:50.873 --> 00:10:52.814
AS I WAS SAYING!

00:10:52.814 --> 00:10:56.289
That potshot promoted you
from least of my concerns.

00:10:57.001 --> 00:10:58.596
Give yourself some credit.

00:10:58.596 --> 00:11:00.048
OH! PERFECT!

00:11:00.048 --> 00:11:01.426
JUST WHO I WANT TO SEE--

00:11:01.426 --> 00:11:03.536
Wait, what the fuck? You're back?

00:11:03.536 --> 00:11:06.044
Are you aiming at me when I turn?

00:11:06.044 --> 00:11:09.037
Wait! What was that?! What
was THAT fucking motion?!

00:11:09.037 --> 00:11:11.156
You'd better not take another shot at me!

00:11:11.156 --> 00:11:11.860
AH?!

00:11:12.411 --> 00:11:13.372
That's what I thought!

00:11:13.372 --> 00:11:16.380
I think this guy might be
hearing voices or something.

00:11:16.380 --> 00:11:16.863
JEE!

00:11:16.863 --> 00:11:18.523
OH YOU WANT SOME?!

00:11:18.523 --> 00:11:19.394
[loud explosion]

00:11:19.394 --> 00:11:20.695
Oh, that's loud...

00:11:20.695 --> 00:11:22.601
So much for lying low.

00:11:22.601 --> 00:11:23.553
I tried.

00:11:23.553 --> 00:11:24.505
[loud explosion]

00:11:24.505 --> 00:11:26.346
Yep. Yep...

00:11:26.346 --> 00:11:30.167
[multiple loud explosions]

00:11:30.167 --> 00:11:32.908
Yeah, that should let
everyone know where I am.

00:11:32.908 --> 00:11:34.767
Any helicopters?

00:11:34.767 --> 00:11:37.770
No? Eh, it'll probably
take them a few minutes.

00:11:37.770 --> 00:11:40.696
I'm still not sure if this
guy's trying to kill me or not.

00:11:40.696 --> 00:11:42.775
I think he might not be sure either.

00:11:42.775 --> 00:11:44.541
Maybe the voices can't decide.

00:11:45.834 --> 00:11:50.713
What he DOES understand is if you're going
to shoot the king, you'd better not miss.

00:11:50.713 --> 00:11:52.664
Come on. Quit crawling around.

00:11:54.685 --> 00:11:56.587
Wow, the car's still burning.

00:11:56.587 --> 00:11:59.178
Yeah, you should be able to
see this from the air nicely.

00:11:59.178 --> 00:12:02.621
At least it's overcast. That
should block me from satellites.

00:12:02.621 --> 00:12:04.496
Or MOST satellites!

00:12:04.496 --> 00:12:09.135
Yeah, dammit, I can't assume anything.
I don't know what technology they have.

00:12:09.135 --> 00:12:14.068
Yeah, wasn't there a Star Trek episode where some
guy goes to the future, tries to scam people,

00:12:14.068 --> 00:12:17.860
but then his ass gets busted because he
doesn't realize what he's up against?

00:12:17.860 --> 00:12:19.500
The fucking future, man...

00:12:19.500 --> 00:12:21.736
I don't even know if
I'm up against that guy.

00:12:21.736 --> 00:12:23.451
What was his name? Gregory?

00:12:23.451 --> 00:12:26.884
His best chance to take me out was
when he told me to turn around,

00:12:26.884 --> 00:12:28.643
but he didn't take the shot.

00:12:28.643 --> 00:12:33.904
So MAYBE he didn't want to, or maybe
he just hesitated. So I don't know!

00:12:33.904 --> 00:12:37.029
Then just now, there WAS
a zombie in front of me.

00:12:37.029 --> 00:12:40.915
Maybe he's the reason hunters are
supposed to wear orange vests.

00:12:40.915 --> 00:12:44.513
Except I AM wearing orange,
so what the fuck?!

00:12:44.513 --> 00:12:48.595
I thought he wouldn't try to kill me
at least until I completed his course,

00:12:48.595 --> 00:12:50.205
but that would imply he's sane.

00:12:50.943 --> 00:12:53.578
He could have competing
voices where one is saying,

00:12:53.578 --> 00:12:58.153
"Wait for him to complete the course." And
the other is saying, "No! Kill him now!"

00:12:58.153 --> 00:12:58.940
GRIGORI: Although they call me crazy--

00:12:58.940 --> 00:12:59.880
OH!

00:12:59.880 --> 00:13:04.611
GRIGORI: I care not, for thou art my
helper, my strength, and my savior.

00:13:04.611 --> 00:13:08.238
That's right. Only gunshots
make the voices go away.

00:13:08.238 --> 00:13:09.954
Well, he's not SO crazy

00:13:09.954 --> 00:13:13.477
that he thinks he can take a shot
at me without plausible deniability.

00:13:13.477 --> 00:13:15.655
He knows I'll kill him if he does that.

00:13:15.655 --> 00:13:18.036
So, you know, neighbors.

00:13:18.036 --> 00:13:20.795
So. What was going on here?

00:13:20.795 --> 00:13:22.161
Was he studying them?

00:13:22.161 --> 00:13:24.357
I bet he doesn't even
have any medical training.

00:13:24.357 --> 00:13:27.684
He was just poking them with a
screwdriver, pretending he's a doctor.

00:13:28.266 --> 00:13:28.900
Oh, for c...

00:13:29.990 --> 00:13:33.926
Yeah, no. I've always wanted a
fan club, but not of YOU people.

00:13:33.926 --> 00:13:35.090
I'm kind of insulted.

00:13:35.090 --> 00:13:36.037
[explosion]

00:13:36.037 --> 00:13:37.684
Apology accepted.

00:13:37.684 --> 00:13:40.477
Oh! It's a long one. All right.

00:13:40.477 --> 00:13:44.050
How did it catch on fire?
I didn't know these were incendiary.

00:13:44.050 --> 00:13:45.540
I just sort of stole them.

00:13:45.540 --> 00:13:48.596
I shouldn't tell Gregory about
this--he might get pissed.

00:13:48.596 --> 00:13:50.746
This could be his private reserve.

00:13:50.746 --> 00:13:53.879
He keeps them penned up in here until
he's ready to start his game show,

00:13:53.879 --> 00:13:54.986
then lets them loose.

00:13:54.986 --> 00:13:58.369
Maybe he really is wrangling
them and trucking them back here.

00:13:58.369 --> 00:14:01.395
But that wouldn't change
the dynamics. Not really.

00:14:01.395 --> 00:14:03.741
Because I was right. Of course.

00:14:03.741 --> 00:14:05.813
Some of these things are going hungry.

00:14:05.813 --> 00:14:06.394
Ah.

00:14:06.394 --> 00:14:08.321
Some of those huggers were skinny.

00:14:08.321 --> 00:14:10.292
Yeah, it's funny--they're facehuggers,

00:14:10.292 --> 00:14:14.167
and I always thought that was the problem
with aliens: They're too good a predator.

00:14:14.167 --> 00:14:18.895
They're smart, they breed fast, their blood
is acid... They would collapse the ecosystem.

00:14:18.895 --> 00:14:19.470
[fast zombies yowling]

00:14:19.470 --> 00:14:20.183
The fuck?

00:14:20.183 --> 00:14:21.476
[fast zombies yowling]

00:14:21.476 --> 00:14:25.141
Okay, I'm impressed with his
show. This is like a circus act.

00:14:26.645 --> 00:14:28.486
AH! GROSS!

00:14:28.486 --> 00:14:29.250
AH!

00:14:31.604 --> 00:14:34.276
I don't even know if this
is part of his show anymore.

00:14:34.645 --> 00:14:35.516
Maybe.

00:14:36.540 --> 00:14:38.686
Before, he was kind of funneling me.

00:14:39.812 --> 00:14:40.766
Ehh...

00:14:40.766 --> 00:14:41.461
[zombie growls]

00:14:41.461 --> 00:14:42.597
Where is that?

00:14:43.119 --> 00:14:44.015
I don't see it.

00:14:44.874 --> 00:14:46.359
More hanging people.

00:14:46.359 --> 00:14:48.324
Well, I guess I have some answers now.

00:14:48.324 --> 00:14:50.699
Like why a body was tied up by the hip.

00:14:50.699 --> 00:14:51.686
He's crazy.

00:14:51.686 --> 00:14:55.448
Or why he's hoarding five washing
machines in a place with no hookups.

00:14:55.448 --> 00:14:56.347
He's crazy.

00:14:56.347 --> 00:14:59.779
That's kind of disappointing, though,
that there's no pattern or meaning.

00:15:01.566 --> 00:15:03.275
It's just some crazy guy?

00:15:04.953 --> 00:15:09.634
It's kind of like when movies make stuff
up, then they say it was all a dream.

00:15:09.634 --> 00:15:10.355
You're not.

00:15:11.772 --> 00:15:14.490
If this was a dream, the
zombies would've turn to Jell-O,

00:15:14.490 --> 00:15:17.565
and when Greg talked, his head would've
floated off because it was a balloon.

00:15:18.475 --> 00:15:19.984
Well, not THAT way.

00:15:21.617 --> 00:15:22.117
Fuck...

00:15:25.337 --> 00:15:26.871
Nyehhh! I WANT THE AMMO!

00:15:26.871 --> 00:15:28.692
[incoherent yelling]

00:15:28.692 --> 00:15:32.232
I'M ACTUALLY GETTING A LITTLE LIGHT
ON BULLETS! I'M NOT PROUD OF THAT!

00:15:32.232 --> 00:15:34.064
BLAH! COME ON WITH THE--

00:15:34.064 --> 00:15:34.564
Fuck...

00:15:35.758 --> 00:15:39.064
THIS IS NOW OFFICIALLY WORSE
THAN MY OLD APARTMENT BUILDING!

00:15:39.064 --> 00:15:40.547
WE'VE CROSSED THAT LINE!

00:15:40.547 --> 00:15:42.111
This isn't a dream!

00:15:42.111 --> 00:15:43.284
Close the door!

00:15:44.214 --> 00:15:45.123
GRIGORI: Here, brother!

00:15:45.123 --> 00:15:46.716
Oh boy...

00:15:46.716 --> 00:15:47.573
GRIGORI: Come closer.

00:15:47.573 --> 00:15:48.872
I'm on a ledge.

00:15:48.872 --> 00:15:50.382
GRIGORI: You've stirred up hell!

00:15:50.382 --> 00:15:51.619
Yeah, yeah.

00:15:51.619 --> 00:15:53.502
GRIGORI: A man after my own heart.

00:15:53.502 --> 00:15:56.431
GRIGORI: Here, I have a
more suitable gun for you.

00:15:56.431 --> 00:15:56.904
GRIGORI: You'll need it.

00:15:56.904 --> 00:15:57.680
Don't do it!

00:15:57.680 --> 00:15:58.345
GRIGORI: Catch!

00:15:58.345 --> 00:15:59.043
Oh!

00:15:59.532 --> 00:16:01.880
GRIGORI: Good. Now keep it close.

00:16:01.880 --> 00:16:02.766
You're a good neighbor.

00:16:02.766 --> 00:16:05.532
GRIGORI: My advice to you
is... aim for the head.

00:16:05.532 --> 00:16:06.521
Yeah, I think--

00:16:06.521 --> 00:16:07.155
GRIGORI: Hush.

00:16:07.155 --> 00:16:07.984
Okay...

00:16:07.984 --> 00:16:08.910
GRIGORI: They come.

00:16:09.608 --> 00:16:10.417
GRIGORI: There is no rest in Ravenholm.

00:16:10.417 --> 00:16:10.917
Uh...

00:16:11.981 --> 00:16:12.648
GRIGROI: Move on and I will...

00:16:12.648 --> 00:16:14.029
Shells, too!

00:16:14.029 --> 00:16:16.254
You're the nicest person I've met today!

00:16:16.254 --> 00:16:17.062
GRIGORI: Woe betide thee...

00:16:17.062 --> 00:16:20.357
Why are these things so amped
up? What are you feeding them?

00:16:20.357 --> 00:16:24.115
Come on. Get indoors. You're
still crazy. You'll catch a cold.

00:16:25.153 --> 00:16:26.580
Yeah, okay!

00:16:26.580 --> 00:16:28.412
See, that was a little close.

00:16:28.412 --> 00:16:31.685
You still have no concept of "line of fire".

00:16:31.685 --> 00:16:33.857
Did you used to be a cop or something?

00:16:33.857 --> 00:16:36.117
Yeah, NOW he's gone. Right.

00:16:36.117 --> 00:16:38.079
So where does he expect me to go?

00:16:38.079 --> 00:16:42.156
Well, he didn't leave a pair of
homemade wings, so that's a positive.

00:16:42.156 --> 00:16:44.509
Oh no. No.

00:16:44.509 --> 00:16:45.583
No, come on.

00:16:45.583 --> 00:16:48.307
He wants me to jump in the
dunk tank like a clown?

00:16:48.307 --> 00:16:50.386
Is he trying to say I'm the clown?

00:16:50.386 --> 00:16:52.807
I am wearing bright colors.

00:16:52.807 --> 00:16:53.753
Fuck.

00:16:56.151 --> 00:16:59.300
I didn't think of it. I should've
checked inside those washers.

00:16:59.300 --> 00:17:02.216
I give a 50-50 chance he
has human heads in there.

00:17:02.216 --> 00:17:03.819
Maybe entire bodies.

00:17:03.819 --> 00:17:05.886
He has to wash the sin out.

